## 6. Testing Limitations

Several limitations were identified during the testing process through Week 3-7:

* Platform and browser/application versions were not recorded consistently for all earlier tests.
* Some earlier testing workflows were not documented at the same level of detail.
* Recovery tests used controlled/distributed corruption rather than uncontrolled real-world transformations.
* Survival rate alone does not indicate whether a hidden message can be successfully decoded.
* Earlier screenshot evidence was collected, but not every screenshot was independently reviewed during the Week 8 review.

---

## 7. Summary of Methodology

Overall, the testing methodology for this project combined compatibility testing with controlled recovery/corruption testing. The platform tests evaluated whether different applications and environments would preserve the encoded zero-width payload, while the recovery tests evaluated the behavior of the improved recovery system under controlled corruption scenarios. Survival rate and decode success were recorded as separate measurements to distinguish payload preservation from successful message recovery. 